            <span class="section-eyebrow">Our Process</span>
            <h2 class="section-title">How to Handle a Copyright Objection from Pune</h2>
            <p class="section-subtitle" style="text-align:left;max-width:100%;">Reply drafting and evidence compilation handled from Patron's Pune office. Reply filed with Copyright Office New Delhi. Hearings require New Delhi attendance (or virtual). Appeals at High Court of Bombay at Pune. Walk-in at Wagholi.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="steps-container">
            <div class="step-card"><div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 1</span><h3 class="step-title">Receive and Analyse the Discrepancy Letter</h3><p class="step-description">When you receive a discrepancy letter from the Registrar of Copyrights, immediately share it with Patron's Pune team. The letter identifies specific objection grounds - similarity with a registered work, authorship claim issues, application defects, or work classification problems. Patron analyses the letter to determine objection type, strength of Registrar's position, and optimal reply strategy. The 30-day clock starts from issuance date.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Grounds Identified</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Strategy Determined</span></div></div><div class="step-visual"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="10" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="25" y="20" width="70" height="15" rx="3" fill="#E8712C" opacity="0.2" stroke="#E8712C" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="60" y="30" font-size="7" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-weight="700">Discrepancy Letter</text><line x1="25" y1="42" x2="95" y2="42" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="60" y="55" font-size="6" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial">Grounds Identified</text><rect x="35" y="62" width="50" height="10" rx="4" fill="#E8712C" opacity="0.15"/><text x="60" y="70" font-size="6" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-weight="600">30 Days Clock</text></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">Analysis Done</span><span class="step-number-large">01</span></div></div></div><div class="step-card"><div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 2</span><h3 class="step-title">Gather Evidence of Originality and Authorship</h3><p class="step-description">Patron works with you to compile evidence supporting your copyright claim - original creation documents, drafts and iterations, timestamps (email records, file metadata, version control logs for software), publication records, and witness statements. For software copyrights in Pune's IT sector, this includes Git commit history, design documents, and architecture specs demonstrating independent creation.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Creation Proof Ready</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Tech Evidence Compiled</span></div></div><div class="step-visual"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="10" y="5" width="100" height="85" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="60" y="22" font-size="7" fill="#E8712C" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-weight="700">Evidence</text><line x1="20" y1="30" x2="100" y2="30" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="0.8"/><rect x="20" y="36" width="80" height="8" rx="3" fill="#FFF3E0" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="60" y="42" font-size="5" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial">Timestamps &amp; Records</text><rect x="20" y="50" width="80" height="8" rx="3" fill="#FFF3E0" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="60" y="56" font-size="5" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial">Code Comparison (IT)</text><rect x="20" y="64" width="80" height="8" rx="3" fill="#FFF3E0" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="60" y="70" font-size="5" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial">Affidavit Prepared</text></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">Evidence Ready</span><span class="step-number-large">02</span></div></div></div><div class="step-card"><div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 3</span><h3 class="step-title">Draft the Reply with Case Law Support</h3><p class="step-description">Patron drafts a comprehensive reply addressing each objection point with factual responses demonstrating originality, legal arguments citing Copyright Act provisions, and case law precedents (Eastern Book Company v D.B. Modak for originality threshold, Tips Industries v Wynk for digital rights, Star India v Leo Burnett for substantial copying). Structured to be persuasive and hearing-robust.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Case Law Cited</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>All Grounds Addressed</span></div></div><div class="step-visual"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="10" y="5" width="100" height="85" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="60" y="22" font-size="7" fill="#E8712C" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-weight="700">Case Law Reply</text><line x1="20" y1="30" x2="100" y2="30" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="25" y="44" font-size="6" fill="#14365F" font-family="Arial">Legal Arguments</text><text x="25" y="56" font-size="6" fill="#14365F" font-family="Arial">Judicial Precedents</text><text x="25" y="68" font-size="6" fill="#14365F" font-family="Arial">Evidence Integrated</text><path d="M90 42l3 3 6-6" stroke="#10B981" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M90 54l3 3 6-6" stroke="#10B981" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M90 66l3 3 6-6" stroke="#10B981" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">Reply Drafted</span><span class="step-number-large">03</span></div></div></div><div class="step-card"><div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 4</span><h3 class="step-title">File the Reply with Supporting Documents</h3><p class="step-description">Reply filed with the Registrar of Copyrights within 30 days (Patron maintains a 2-day buffer) along with original application copy, discrepancy letter, supporting evidence, affidavit (if required), and Power of Attorney. Filing through Copyright Office portal or by post to New Delhi. Patron tracks filing confirmation.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Filed Before Deadline</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>2-Day Buffer Met</span></div></div><div class="step-visual"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="10" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="60" y="30" font-size="7" fill="#E8712C" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-weight="700">Filed by Day 28</text><text x="60" y="48" font-size="6" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial">Copyright Office NDelhi</text><rect x="35" y="56" width="50" height="12" rx="4" fill="#10B981" opacity="0.2"/><text x="60" y="65" font-size="6" fill="#10B981" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-weight="700">2-Day Buffer</text></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">Reply Filed</span><span class="step-number-large">04</span></div></div></div><div class="step-card"><div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 5</span><h3 class="step-title">Attend Hearing (If Scheduled)</h3><p class="step-description">If the Registrar is not satisfied with the written reply, a hearing may be scheduled. Patron coordinates with IP advocates for representation before the Copyright Office in New Delhi. Hearing brief prepared with arguments, evidence bundles, and oral argument outlines. Both applicant and objecting party present their cases.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Brief Prepared</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Advocate Represents</span></div></div><div class="step-visual"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="15" y="10" width="90" height="70" rx="6" fill="#F0F4F8" stroke="#14365F" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="25" y="22" width="70" height="15" rx="4" fill="#FFF3E0" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="60" y="32" font-size="7" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-weight="600">Hearing Brief</text><text x="60" y="52" font-size="6" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial">Arguments Presented</text><text x="60" y="64" font-size="6" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial">IP Advocate Represents</text></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">Hearing Attended</span><span class="step-number-large">05</span></div></div></div><div class="step-card"><div class="step-content"><span class="step-badge">Step 6</span><h3 class="step-title">Resolution and Registration Completion</h3><p class="step-description">If the objection is resolved in your favour, the Registrar proceeds with copyright registration - entering the work in the Register of Copyrights and issuing the certificate. If the decision is adverse, Patron advises on appeal at the High Court of Bombay at Pune. Related: <a href="/copyright-assignment/pune">Copyright Assignment in Pune</a>.</p><div class="step-highlights"><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Objection Set Aside</span><span class="highlight-tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Certificate Issued</span></div></div><div class="step-visual"><div class="step-illustration"><div class="illustration-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="20" y="15" width="80" height="30" rx="4" fill="#10B981" opacity="0.15"/><text x="60" y="33" font-size="8" fill="#10B981" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-weight="700">Objection Resolved</text><rect x="25" y="55" width="70" height="25" rx="4" fill="#FFF3E0" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="0.8"/><text x="60" y="70" font-size="7" fill="#14365F" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-weight="600">Certificate Issued</text></svg></div><span class="illustration-label">Registration Complete</span><span class="step-number-large">06</span></div></div></div>

